SkyLink-Analysis-By-Power-BI
📘 Project Overview
As a Business Intelligence Analyst at Gulf Researcher, you are tasked with analyzing customer churn rates for SkyLink, a telecommunication company. The goal of this project is to uncover the reasons behind customer churn and provide actionable insights to reduce it. Using Microsoft Power BI, a visually compelling interactive dashboard was developed to help SkyLink better understand and manage customer churn.

This analysis addresses specific business questions raised by SkyLink and focuses on identifying key drivers of churn to enhance retention strategies.

🧼 Data Cleaning (Transformation)
Churn Category: Replaced blank values with "No Churning".
Churn Reason: Replaced blank values with "No Reason As No Churning".
New Column: Created a column to mark whether the customer has churned (Churn Label = "Yes"), simplifying churn-related calculations.
📊 Key Analysis & Business Questions
1. 🔢 Current Churn Rate
Formula: (Total Churned Customers / Total Customers) * 100
Churn Rate = 30.6%
Shown using a pie chart with CustomerID and Churn Label.
2. 🏷 Churn Categories
The most common churn category is "Competitor".
3. 🗺 Churn Rate by State
Churn varies significantly by state.
Highest churn rate is in: California (CA).
4. 🎂 Churn Rate by Age Group
Under 30: 26.15%
Over 65: 43.44%
Insight: Churn increases with age.
5. 👥 Churn by Group Size
Group size = 3 has the lowest churn rate = 5.63%.
6. 🧾 Contract Type vs. Churn
Customers with monthly contracts churn the most.
Customers with two-year contracts churn the least.
7. 📶 Unlimited Data Plan Impact
Customers without unlimited plans are more likely to churn.
Churn rate peaks when data usage hits 41 GB.
8. 🌍 International Activity & Churn
Higher international usage is linked to higher churn rates.
9. 👤 Customer Profile Insights
Payment Method:
Direct Debit → Higher churn
Paper Check → Lower churn
Contract Type:
Monthly → More churn
Two-Year → Less churn
Account Length:
Shorter duration → Higher churn
🧮 Specific Measures & Deep Dives
🎯 Targeted Group Churn
Customers not in a group, aged 50, account ≤ 12 months
→ Churn Rate = 48.57%
📞 Service Calls & Churn
Avg. number of service calls for customers on:
Monthly contract + Direct Debit = 1.57
Churn Rate for same group = 58.47%
💸 Extra Data Charges
Customers without unlimited data, consuming ≥10GB
→ Average extra data charge = $30.20
🛠 Tools Used
Microsoft Power BI
Microsoft Excel
